 "<a href=\"#metric\">Breadth and depth</a>": "<a href=\"#metric\">广度与深度</a>",
 "<a href=\"#results\">Sixteen agents</a>": "<a href=\"#results\">十六个智能体的结果</a>",
 "<a href=\"#domains\">Across 24 domains</a>": "<a href=\"#domains\">二十四个领域</a>",
 "<a href=\"#process\">From retrieval to report</a>": "<a href=\"#process\">从检索到报告</a>",
 "<a href=\"#trust\">Can the scores be trusted?</a>": "<a href=\"#trust\">评分是否可信</a>",
 "<a href=\"#use\">Evaluate your own agent</a>": "<a href=\"#use\">评测自己的智能体</a>",
 "Give a deep research agent an open question and it plans, searches, reads and writes a long report. To judge the report, we have to ask what it covered. Most benchmarks answer with a list of rubrics and a count of how many the report satisfies. A count cannot tell a report that touches every direction lightly from one that follows a few directions all the way down.": "向深度研究智能体提出一个开放问题，它会规划、检索、阅读，最后写出一份长篇报告。评价这份报告，首先要回答它覆盖了哪些内容。多数评测基准的做法是列出一组评分细则，统计报告满足了几条。但计数无法区分两种报告：一种在每个方向上都只点到为止，另一种沿少数方向一路深挖。",
 "DRBench Pro keeps that structure. Each case is built from a knowledge tree grown out of a Wikipedia article. The children of the root are <strong>research directions</strong>; the paths below them, up to three hops, are <strong>chains of related knowledge</strong>. Every edge of the tree becomes one rubric grounded in Wikipedia evidence. The agent receives only a research question written from the same tree; the tree and its rubrics stay hidden. A judge checks each rubric against the report, and the verdicts are combined from the leaves up into <strong>breadth</strong>, how fully the directions are covered, and <strong>depth</strong>, how far the chains are followed. <strong>Overall coverage</strong> is their geometric mean.": "DRBench Pro 保留了这种结构。每个样例都源自一棵由维基百科条目扩展而成的知识树：根节点的子节点是<strong>研究方向</strong>，其下最多三跳的路径是<strong>相关知识链</strong>。树中每条边对应一条以维基百科证据为依据的评分细则。智能体只拿到根据这棵树写成的研究问题，树本身和评分细则都不可见。评判模型逐条对照报告给出判定，再从叶节点向上汇总为<strong>广度</strong>和<strong>深度</strong>：广度衡量各方向覆盖得是否全面，深度衡量知识链追踪得有多远。<strong>总体覆盖率</strong>取两者的几何平均。",
 "<strong>On 144 cases across 24 domains (44,102 rubrics), the best of 16 agents, Claude Opus 5, reaches 57.04% overall coverage. Breadth and depth rank the agents differently, and the same model changes its profile when the research workflow around it changes.</strong>": "<strong>在 24 个领域的 144 个样例（共 44,102 条评分细则）上，16 个智能体中表现最好的 Claude Opus 5 总体覆盖率为 57.04%。广度与深度给出的排名并不一致，同一模型在不同研究流程下的覆盖特征也会明显变化。</strong>",
 "<a class=\"card\" href=\"#results\"><p class=\"card-k\">Overall coverage, all 144 cases</p><p class=\"card-t\">Even the best covers just over half</p><div class=\"card-chart\" data-card=\"0\"></div></a> <a class=\"card\" href=\"#results\"><p class=\"card-k\">Qwen3.8 Max, breadth</p><p class=\"card-t\">Same model, different workflow, different profile</p><div class=\"card-chart\" data-card=\"1\"></div></a> <a class=\"card\" href=\"#process\"><p class=\"card-k\">Retrieved knowledge that reaches the report, mean of seven backbones</p><p class=\"card-t\">Deeper knowledge is dropped more often</p><div class=\"card-chart\" data-card=\"2\"></div></a> <a class=\"card\" href=\"#trust\"><p class=\"card-k\">Agreement with expert rankings (Kendall τ<sub>b</sub>, overall)</p><p class=\"card-t\">Structure brings scores closer to experts</p><div class=\"card-chart\" data-card=\"3\"></div></a>": "<a class=\"card\" href=\"#results\"><p class=\"card-k\">总体覆盖率，全部 144 个样例</p><p class=\"card-t\">最好的智能体也只覆盖一半多</p><div class=\"card-chart\" data-card=\"0\"></div></a> <a class=\"card\" href=\"#results\"><p class=\"card-k\">Qwen3.8 Max 的广度</p><p class=\"card-t\">同一模型，流程不同，特征不同</p><div class=\"card-chart\" data-card=\"1\"></div></a> <a class=\"card\" href=\"#process\"><p class=\"card-k\">检索到的知识进入报告的比例，七个基座模型的平均</p><p class=\"card-t\">知识越深，越容易在写作中丢失</p><div class=\"card-chart\" data-card=\"2\"></div></a> <a class=\"card\" href=\"#trust\"><p class=\"card-k\">与专家排序的一致性（Kendall τ<sub>b</sub>，总体）</p><p class=\"card-t\">保留结构，评分更接近专家判断</p><div class=\"card-chart\" data-card=\"3\"></div></a>",
 "<span class=\"n\">1</span>A count hides the shape": "<span class=\"n\">1</span>计数掩盖了结构",
 "Deep research questions are open-ended. Many different reports can answer one well, and no single reference answer holds everything relevant. Fact-checking tells us whether what a report says is supported; it cannot tell us what the report left out. Benchmarks therefore write down the expected content, from expert reports, reference facts or rubrics, and check the report against it. Coverage is then usually one score among several, next to writing, citation and formatting, and the rubrics are added up flat: every satisfied item counts the same.": "深度研究问题是开放的：好的回答可以有很多种，任何单一的参考答案都无法囊括全部相关知识。事实核查能判断报告中的陈述是否有依据，却无法发现报告遗漏了什么。因此，评测基准通常先写明期望的内容，来源包括专家报告、参考事实或评分细则，再据此检查报告。覆盖度往往只是写作、引用、格式等多项评分中的一项，而且评分细则是平铺累加的：满足任何一条都计同样的分。",
 "Adding them up flat throws away how the items relate. Take three reports on the same question that each satisfy the same number of rubrics. The first states the opening fact of every direction and stops there. The second follows two directions down to their deepest facts and ignores the rest. The third picks up scattered details deep in the tree without the links that connect them. They read differently and serve different readers, yet a count gives all three the same score. <a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-2\">Figure 2</a> lets you build such reports and watch what happens.": "平铺累加丢掉了条目之间的关系。设想针对同一问题的三份报告，各自满足的评分细则数量相同。第一份只写出每个方向开头的事实；第二份沿两个方向一直写到最深处，其余方向一概不提；第三份零散地提到树中较深的细节，却缺少把它们串起来的中间环节。三份报告读起来不同，适合的读者也不同，计数却给出同样的分数。<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-2\">图 2</a> 可以动手构造这样的报告，观察分数的变化。",
 "DRBench Pro makes <strong>structured knowledge coverage</strong> the main thing it measures. That takes three parts: a reference space whose structure is known, rubrics that each sit at a known position in it, and a metric that uses those positions.": "DRBench Pro 把<strong>结构化知识覆盖</strong>作为核心评测对象。这需要三个条件：结构已知的参考空间，在其中位置明确的评分细则，以及利用这些位置的评测指标。",
 "<span class=\"n\">2</span>From a Wikipedia tree to hidden rubrics": "<span class=\"n\">2</span>从维基百科知识树到隐藏的评分细则",
 "<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-1\">Figure 1</a> walks through one case from the paper. The root is the Wikipedia article <em>Roguelike</em>; the figure follows 12 of the rubrics in two of its ten directions, with the judge’s actual verdicts on a report written by o3 Deep Research.": "<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#fig-1\">图 1</a> 逐步演示论文中的一个样例。根节点是维基百科条目 <em>Roguelike</em>；图中选取其十个研究方向中两个方向下的 12 条评分细则，判定结果均为评判模型对 o3 Deep Research 所写报告的实际判定。",
 "<span class=\"d1-tn\">1</span>Build the tree<i class=\"d1-prog\"></i>": "<span class=\"d1-tn\">1</span>构建知识树<i class=\"d1-prog\"></i>",
 "<span class=\"d1-tn\">2</span>Ask the question<i class=\"d1-prog\"></i>": "<span class=\"d1-tn\">2</span>生成研究问题<i class=\"d1-prog\"></i>",
 "<span class=\"d1-tn\">3</span>Score the report<i class=\"d1-prog\"></i>": "<span class=\"d1-tn\">3</span>为报告评分<i class=\"d1-prog\"></i>",
 "Build a local knowledge tree": "构建局部知识树",
 "<span class=\"d1-k\">Root</span><span class=\"d1-w\">W</span> Roguelike <span class=\"d1-dom\">Games domain</span>": "<span class=\"d1-k\">根节点</span><span class=\"d1-w\">W</span> Roguelike <span class=\"d1-dom\">游戏领域</span>",
 "<span class=\"d1-k\">Expand</span>Follow Wikipedia links breadth-first; each edge is a relation stated in the source article.": "<span class=\"d1-k\">扩展</span>沿维基百科链接广度优先扩展，每条边都是源条目中陈述的一种关系。",
 "<b>Hop 1</b><span>50 children of the root</span>": "<b>第 1 跳</b><span>根节点保留 50 个子节点</span>",
 "<b>Hop 2</b><span>up to 5 children per node</span>": "<b>第 2 跳</b><span>每个节点最多 5 个子节点</span>",
 "<b>Hop 3</b><span>stop; about 1.5K nodes per tree</span>": "<b>第 3 跳</b><span>停止扩展；每棵树约 1.5K 个节点</span>",
 "<span class=\"d1-k\">Sample</span>A case keeps the root and <b>10 complete branches</b> that fit one research task. This one keeps Dungeons &amp; Dragons, Rogue, ASCII, Colossal Cave Adventure and six more. We follow two of them.": "<span class=\"d1-k\">采样</span>每个样例保留根节点和<b>10 个完整分支</b>，共同对应一项研究任务。本例保留了 Dungeons &amp; Dragons、Rogue、ASCII、Colossal Cave Adventure 等十个分支，图中展示其中两个。",
 "One subgraph, one question, many rubrics": "同一子图，生成一个问题和多条评分细则",
 "<span class=\"d1-k\">Research query</span><span class=\"fx-type\" data-a=\"9300\" data-b=\"11700\">I’m trying to understand the origins of the roguelike video game genre … how the hardware and display limitations of the era shaped its distinctive look, and how tabletop role-playing traditions fed into its dungeon-crawling structure.</span>": "<span class=\"d1-k\">研究问题</span><span class=\"fx-type\" data-a=\"9300\" data-b=\"11700\">I’m trying to understand the origins of the roguelike video game genre … how the hardware and display limitations of the era shaped its distinctive look, and how tabletop role-playing traditions fed into its dungeon-crawling structure.</span>",
 "<span class=\"d1-k\">One rubric per edge</span><span class=\"d1-rid\">R9</span> The report explicitly states or clearly paraphrases that Ken Arnold wrote the first curses library, released with BSD UNIX and used for games such as Rogue.": "<span class=\"d1-k\">每条边一条评分细则</span><span class=\"d1-rid\">R9</span> The report explicitly states or clearly paraphrases that Ken Arnold wrote the first curses library, released with BSD UNIX and used for games such as Rogue.",
 "<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" viewbox=\"0 0 16 16\"><rect fill=\"currentColor\" height=\"7\" rx=\"1.5\" width=\"10\" x=\"3\" y=\"7\"></rect><path d=\"M5.5 7V5a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 5 0v2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"></path></svg><span>The tree and its rubrics stay hidden. The agent sees only the query.</span>": "<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" viewbox=\"0 0 16 16\"><rect fill=\"currentColor\" height=\"7\" rx=\"1.5\" width=\"10\" x=\"3\" y=\"7\"></rect><path d=\"M5.5 7V5a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 5 0v2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"></path></svg><span>知识树和评分细则均不公开，智能体只能看到研究问题。</span>",
 "o3 Deep Research writes a report": "o3 Deep Research 撰写报告",
 "Early Inspirations: D&amp;D and the First Digital Dungeon Crawls": "Early Inspirations: D&amp;D and the First Digital Dungeon Crawls",
 "Text-Only Technology and ASCII Art Dungeons": "Text-Only Technology and ASCII Art Dungeons",
 "Procedural Generation, Challenge, and “Perma-Death”": "Procedural Generation, Challenge, and “Perma-Death”",
 "The Birth of Rogue and its Founding Developers": "The Birth of Rogue and its Founding Developers",
 "Parallel Evolution: Early Roguelike Variants …": "Parallel Evolution: Early Roguelike Variants …",
 "Judge each rubric, then aggregate up the tree": "逐条判定，再沿树向上汇总",
 "<span class=\"d1-rid\" id=\"d1-jid\">R1</span><span id=\"d1-jrel\">Roguelike → Rogue</span><span class=\"d1-verdict\" id=\"d1-jv\"></span>": "<span class=\"d1-rid\" id=\"d1-jid\">R1</span><span id=\"d1-jrel\">Roguelike → Rogue</span><span class=\"d1-verdict\" id=\"d1-jv\"></span>",
 "<span>Breadth</span><i><b></b></i><em>0.90</em>": "<span>广度</span><i><b></b></i><em>0.90</em>",
 "<span>Depth</span><i><b></b></i><em>0.79</em>": "<span>深度</span><i><b></b></i><em>0.79</em>",
 "<span>Overall</span><i><b></b></i><em>0.84</em>": "<span>总体</span><i><b></b></i><em>0.84</em>",
 "Two misses, two different costs. Missing R6 leaves Hack with no deeper chain; missing R12 stops the Beneath Apple Manor chain one hop short.": "两处缺失，代价不同：缺少 R6，Hack 之下没有更深的知识链；缺少 R12，Beneath Apple Manor 这条链差一跳未能走完。",
 "<b>Figure 1.</b> One case, step by step: the <em>Roguelike</em> knowledge tree, the query generated from it, and the judge’s verdicts on a report by o3 Deep Research (paper Appendix E.4, Figure 10 and Table 25). The 12 rubrics are a representative subset of the 60 in two of the case’s ten directions; the full case has 308. The node values in the last step (breadth / depth) and the three scores treat these two directions as if they were the whole case, to show how the metric works. Evidence quotes are from the report. Click a stage to jump to it.": "<b>图 1：</b>逐步演示一个样例：<em>Roguelike</em> 知识树、由其生成的研究问题，以及评判模型对 o3 Deep Research 报告的判定（对应论文附录 E.4 的图 10 与表 25）。图中 12 条评分细则选自该样例十个方向中的两个方向，这两个方向共有 60 条，整个样例共 308 条。最后一步中的节点数值（广度 / 深度）和三项得分把这两个方向视为完整样例计算，仅用于说明指标的计算方式。证据引文摘自报告原文。点击上方阶段可直接跳转。",
 "Growing the tree": "构建知识树",
 "The 24 domains are the topic categories of WebOrganizer, and each has two root entities, such as <em>Xerox Alto</em> and <em>Cray-1</em> for hardware or <em>Ignaz Semmelweis</em> and <em>John Snow</em> for health. From each root, Wikipedia links are expanded breadth-first. Nodes are entities, and an edge is a relationship supported by a link anchor and the text around it. The expansion is kept as a rooted tree, so every node has one parent and every relation has one position. It stops at three hops, keeping 50 children of the root and at most five children of every other node; Claude Opus 4.8 picks them for relevance and research value. The 48 trees have about 1.5K nodes each.": "24 个领域取自 WebOrganizer 的主题分类，每个领域选两个根实体，例如硬件领域的 <em>Xerox Alto</em> 和 <em>Cray-1</em>，健康领域的 <em>Ignaz Semmelweis</em> 和 <em>John Snow</em>。从每个根实体出发，沿维基百科链接广度优先扩展。节点是实体，边是由链接锚文本及其上下文支撑的关系。扩展结果保存为有根树，每个节点只有一个父节点，每条关系都有确定的位置。扩展在第三跳停止，根节点保留 50 个子节点，其余节点最多保留 5 个，由 Claude Opus 4.8 按相关性和研究价值挑选。48 棵树平均各有约 1.5K 个节点。",
 "Sampling a research scope": "采样研究范围",
 "A whole tree is more than one research request can reasonably ask for. A <strong>branch</strong>, one child of the root with all its descendants, is a research direction. Each case keeps the root and <strong>10 complete branches</strong> that together give complementary angles on one research task, and each root yields three cases with no shared branches. That gives 144 cases. We first built 720 cases and evaluated three deep research systems on them. Keeping two roots per domain left 96.7% of the sampled scores within two points of the full pool, and kept the systems’ order in all 20 samples, so the benchmark uses two roots per domain.": "一整棵树的内容远超一次研究请求的合理范围。根节点的一个子节点连同其全部后代构成一个<strong>分支</strong>，即一个研究方向。每个样例保留根节点和<strong>10 个完整分支</strong>，它们从互补的角度服务于同一项研究任务；每个根实体生成三个样例，样例之间不共享分支，共得到 144 个样例。我们最初构建了 720 个样例，并在其上评测了三个深度研究系统。每个领域保留两个根实体时，96.7% 的抽样得分与完整样例池的差距在两个百分点以内，20 次抽样中系统排序全部保持不变，因此基准最终采用每领域两个根实体。",
 "One query, many hidden rubrics": "一个问题，多条隐藏的评分细则",
 "The query and the rubrics come from the same subgraph. The query is a natural research request about the root and the broader themes of the sampled branches; the prompt discourages listing the hidden entities, so the agent has to investigate a topic rather than fill in an outline. Then every retained edge becomes one rubric, asking whether the report covers the relationship between its two entities. The rubric is written only from the supplied evidence: the two pages’ summaries, the anchor sentence, the relevant paragraphs and the backlink context. A case has 236 to 310 rubrics, 306 on average, and 80.45% of them sit at the third hop.": "研究问题和评分细则出自同一个子图。研究问题是一段自然的研究请求，围绕根实体和所采样分支的总体主题展开；提示词要求不要罗列隐藏的实体，因此智能体需要自行调研，而不是照着提纲填空。随后，每条保留的边生成一条评分细则，检查报告是否写到了这条边两端实体之间的关系。评分细则只依据给定的证据撰写：两个页面的摘要、锚文本所在句、相关段落和反向链接上下文。每个样例有 236 至 310 条评分细则，平均 306 条，其中 80.45% 位于第三跳。",
 "To score a report, a judge (Gemini 2.5 Pro) gives each rubric one of three verdicts: Satisfied, Partially Satisfied or Not Satisfied. Only Satisfied counts as covered. <a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#trust\">Section 7</a> explains why the scores use this binary mapping.": "评分时，评判模型（Gemini 2.5 Pro）对每条评分细则给出三种判定之一：满足、部分满足、不满足。只有“满足”计为覆盖。<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#trust\">第 7 节</a>说明了采用这种二值映射的原因。",
 "<span class=\"n\">3</span>Breadth and depth": "<span class=\"n\">3</span>广度与深度",
 "Both metrics are computed from the leaves up. Each relation <span class=\"mi\">v</span> has a verdict <span class=\"mi\">x(v)</span> of 1 (covered) or 0, and a leaf starts with <span class=\"mi\">B = D = x</span>.": "两项指标都从叶节点向上计算。每条关系 <span class=\"mi\">v</span> 有一个判定值 <span class=\"mi\">x(v)</span>，覆盖为 1，否则为 0；叶节点的初值为 <span class=\"mi\">B = D = x</span>。",
 "<strong>Breadth</strong> asks how fully the directions are covered. At an inner node, it mixes the relation’s own verdict with the mean breadth of its children:": "<strong>广度</strong>衡量各方向覆盖得是否全面。在内部节点上，它把该关系自身的判定与子节点广度的均值加权组合：",
 "<span class=\"mi\">B(v) = β·x(v) + (1 − β)·mean B(children)</span>, with β = 0.6.": "<span class=\"mi\">B(v) = β·x(v) + (1 − β)·mean B(children)</span>，其中 β = 0.6。",
 "Covering a relation alone therefore does not earn full credit for everything below it, while covered descendants partly make up for a missing relation above them. Case breadth is the plain mean over the ten directions, so a direction with more rubrics does not count for more.": "因此，只写到某条关系并不能拿到其下整棵子树的全部分数；反过来，后代被覆盖也能部分弥补上层关系的缺失。样例的广度是十个方向的简单平均，评分细则多的方向不会占更大权重。",
 "<strong>Depth</strong> asks how far chains are followed. The children’s depth values are sorted, and the best one gets the most weight: weights fall by a factor ρ = 0.5 per rank and are normalized, giving <span class=\"mi\">d(v)</span>. Then": "<strong>深度</strong>衡量知识链追踪得有多远。子节点的深度值先排序，最好的一条权重最大：权重按名次以 ρ = 0.5 的比例递减并归一化，得到 <span class=\"mi\">d(v)</span>。然后",
 "<span class=\"mi\">D(v) = α·x(v) + (1 − α)·d(v)·[η + (1 − η)·x(v)]</span>, with α = 0.25 and η = 0.75.": "<span class=\"mi\">D(v) = α·x(v) + (1 − α)·d(v)·[η + (1 − η)·x(v)]</span>，其中 α = 0.25，η = 0.75。",
 "The bracket rewards continuity. If the relation linking a node to its parent is covered, the evidence below it counts in full; if it is missing, that evidence is multiplied by 0.75, discounted but not thrown away. Case depth applies the same rank weighting across the ten directions. <strong>Overall coverage</strong> is <span class=\"mi\">√(B·D)</span> for each case, so a weak score in either dimension pulls it down. The three metrics are then averaged over cases separately.": "方括号一项奖励连续性：如果节点与父节点之间的关系被覆盖，其下的证据全额计入；如果这条关系缺失，其下的证据乘以 0.75，打折但不清零。样例的深度在十个方向上采用同样的按名次加权。每个样例的<strong>总体覆盖率</strong>为 <span class=\"mi\">√(B·D)</span>，任一维度偏弱都会拉低总分。三项指标最后分别在所有样例上取平均。",
 "<b>Figure 2.</b> A small tree with four directions and 28 rubrics. The three example reports each cover 12 rubrics, so a flat count scores them all 12/28 = 0.43. Breadth and depth tell them apart: the first two land on nearly the same overall coverage from opposite profiles. The scattered report covers relations at different levels across directions, with some deeper relations missing the links above them. It scores lowest among the three examples. Click any node to toggle its rubric; the scores use the benchmark’s own parameters.": "<b>图 2：</b>一棵有四个方向、28 条评分细则的小树。三份示例报告各覆盖 12 条，按平铺计数都得 12/28 = 0.43。广度与深度能把它们区分开：前两份的总体覆盖率几乎相同，但特征截然相反。第三份报告在不同方向覆盖了不同层级的关系，部分深层关系缺少对应的上层关系。它在三个示例中得分最低。点击任意节点可切换其评分细则的覆盖状态，得分按基准的实际参数计算。",
 "<span class=\"n\">4</span>Sixteen agents": "<span class=\"n\">4</span>十六个智能体的结果",
 "We evaluate 16 agents in three groups, distinguished by who provides search and research orchestration.": "我们评测了 16 个智能体，按检索与研究流程由谁提供分为三组。",
 "<strong>Deep research systems</strong>, built for long, autonomous investigations: o3 Deep Research, Perplexity Sonar Deep Research and Qwen Deep Research.": "<strong>深度研究系统</strong>，面向长时间自主调研设计：o3 Deep Research、Perplexity Sonar Deep Research 和 Qwen Deep Research。",
 "<strong>Native search LLMs</strong>, which call the provider’s own web search during generation: Claude Opus 5, Grok 4.5, GPT-5.6 Sol, Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview, Sonar Reasoning Pro and Qwen3.8 Max.": "<strong>原生搜索大模型</strong>，在生成过程中调用服务商自带的网页搜索：Claude Opus 5、Grok 4.5、GPT-5.6 Sol、Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview、Sonar Reasoning Pro 和 Qwen3.8 Max。",
 "<strong>Backbone LLMs in a local research framework</strong>: the same fixed Wikipedia snapshot, the same Search and Open tools, the same workflow and the same budget, with provider search turned off (<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#process\">Section 6</a>). Seven backbones: Qwen3.8 Max, MiniMax M3, GLM 5.2, DeepSeek V4 Flash, DeepSeek V4 Pro, Qwen3.7 Plus and Gemma 4 31B.": "<strong>本地研究框架中的基座模型</strong>：使用同一份固定的维基百科快照、同样的 Search 和 Open 工具、同样的流程和预算，并关闭服务商自带搜索（见<a class=\"fig-ref\" href=\"#process\">第 6 节</a>）。共七个基座模型：Qwen3.8 Max、MiniMax M3、GLM 5.2、DeepSeek V4 Flash、DeepSeek V4 Pro、Qwen3.7 Plus 和 Gemma 4 31B。",
 "<b>Figure 3.</b> Main results on all 144 cases (paper Table 2, %). Switch the metric to watch the order change. System overall coverage is the mean of the case-level scores, not the geometric mean of the mean breadth and mean depth shown here.": "<b>图 3：</b>全部 144 个样例上的主要结果（对应论文表 2，单位为 %）。切换指标可以看到排序的变化。系统的总体覆盖率是各样例得分的平均，并非图中平均广度与平均深度的几何平均。",
 "<strong>Claude Opus 5 is first on all three metrics</strong>: 57.04% overall, 53.09% breadth and 61.91% depth. Grok 4.5 is second overall (50.98%) and second in breadth, but fifth in depth; o3 Deep Research is third overall and second in depth. Everyone else interleaves. Perplexity Sonar Deep Research is third in depth and eleventh in breadth. Even the best agent leaves more than 40% of the expected knowledge uncovered.": "<strong>Claude Opus 5 在三项指标上均排名第一</strong>：总体覆盖率 57.04%，广度 53.09%，深度 61.91%。Grok 4.5 总体第二（50.98%），广度也是第二，深度却排第五；o3 Deep Research 总体第三，深度第二。其余智能体的排名相互交错：Perplexity Sonar Deep Research 深度第三，广度却只排第十一。即使是最好的智能体，也有四成以上的期望知识没有覆盖。",
 "The workflow around a model matters as much as the model. Qwen3.8 Max in the local research framework scores 15.54 points higher in breadth and 6.28 points higher in depth than the same model with its native search. The framework makes it plan three research units and check for gaps, and most of the gain is in breadth. Within the Perplexity family, the deep research product beats Sonar Reasoning Pro in depth (54.08 vs. 50.24) and is slightly behind it in breadth (40.00 vs. 40.86). Among the backbones that share the local framework, breadth scores at the top are already close, and depth separates them.": "模型所处的研究流程与模型本身同样重要。在本地研究框架中，Qwen3.8 Max 的广度比使用自带搜索时高 15.54 个百分点，深度高 6.28 个百分点。该框架要求模型规划三个研究单元并检查覆盖缺口，提升主要体现在广度上。在 Perplexity 的产品中，深度研究产品的深度高于 Sonar Reasoning Pro（54.08 对 50.24），广度则略低（40.00 对 40.86）。在共享本地框架的基座模型中，排名靠前者的广度已经相近，拉开差距的是深度。",
 "Same score, different reports": "分数相同，报告不同",
 "Aggregates hide the most at the level of a single case. On the case about the British media mogul <em>Lew Grade</em>, Perplexity Sonar Deep Research and Grok 4.5 get almost the same overall coverage, 38.83% and 40.31%, with mirrored profiles: Perplexity follows a few chains far (breadth 27.33%, depth 55.19%), while Grok touches most directions but stays shallow (breadth 54.48%, depth 29.82%). On the <em>temperance movement</em>, o3 Deep Research and GPT-5.6 Sol agree even on breadth and depth (32.11 vs. 34.64, 48.26 vs. 50.43), yet at the level of single directions their reports go down different chains of the same tree.": "在单个样例上，汇总分数掩盖的差异最大。以英国传媒大亨 <em>Lew Grade</em> 为题的样例中，Perplexity Sonar Deep Research 和 Grok 4.5 的总体覆盖率几乎相同，分别为 38.83% 和 40.31%，覆盖特征却恰好相反：Perplexity 沿少数知识链走得很远（广度 27.33%，深度 55.19%），Grok 覆盖了多数方向但停留在浅层（广度 54.48%，深度 29.82%）。在<em>禁酒运动</em>样例上，o3 Deep Research 和 GPT-5.6 Sol 的广度和深度都很接近（32.11 对 34.64，48.26 对 50.43），但具体到各个方向，两份报告沿着同一棵树上不同的知识链展开。",
 "<b>Figure 4.</b> Breadth against depth. The dashed curves join points with equal √(B·D), so points on one curve have the same case-level overall coverage. Left: the 16 agents’ mean scores. The two case views show single reports from paper Figure 3 and Appendix E. Hover a point for its values.": "<b>图 4：</b>广度与深度的关系。虚线连接 √(B·D) 相等的点，同一条曲线上的点具有相同的样例级总体覆盖率。默认视图为 16 个智能体的平均得分；两个样例视图展示论文图 3 与附录 E 中的单份报告。鼠标悬停于数据点可查看数值。",
 "<span class=\"n\">5</span>Across 24 domains": "<span class=\"n\">5</span>二十四个领域",
 "Coverage also depends on the subject. Averaged over agents, it is highest in Software Development (53.69%), Science &amp; Technology (52.36%) and Health (50.10%), and lowest in Industrial (28.58%) and Food &amp; Dining (35.45%). Claude Opus 5 leads in 23 of the 24 domains; the exception is Literature, where o3 Deep Research leads with 53.2% against 49.6%.": "覆盖率也与主题有关。按智能体平均，覆盖率最高的是软件开发（53.69%）、科学与技术（52.36%）和健康（50.10%），最低的是工业（28.58%）和餐饮（35.45%）。Claude Opus 5 在 24 个领域中的 23 个领先，唯一的例外是文学领域，o3 Deep Research 以 53.2% 对 49.6% 领先。",
 "<b>Figure 5.</b> Overall coverage (%) for each agent and domain, each cell averaged over the domain’s six cases (paper Figure 4). Outlined cells are the best agent in their row. The last column is the mean over agents. Hover a cell for details.": "<b>图 5：</b>各智能体在各领域的总体覆盖率（%），每格为该领域六个样例的平均（对应论文图 4）。加框的单元格是该行最好的智能体，最后一列是所有智能体的平均。鼠标悬停于单元格可查看详情。",
 "<span class=\"n\">6</span>From retrieval to report": "<span class=\"n\">6</span>从检索到报告",
 "Comparing products tells us which one covers more, but not why. For a controlled comparison, the local research framework fixes everything except the backbone model. Retrieval runs offline over one English Wikipedia snapshot (enwiki-20260701-v1) through two tools, <code>Search</code> and <code>Open</code>. The model splits the query into three research units that gather evidence in parallel, runs one coverage-gap check that may launch one extra gap unit, and writes the report. The search budget and the workflow are the same for every backbone, and so is the evidence space, which does not drift over time. That leaves planning, tool use, evidence selection and writing to the model, and every trajectory can be audited.": "比较不同产品能看出谁覆盖得多，却看不出原因。为进行受控比较，本地研究框架固定了基座模型以外的所有因素。检索在一份英文维基百科快照（enwiki-20260701-v1）上离线进行，只提供 <code>Search</code> 和 <code>Open</code> 两个工具。模型把问题拆成三个并行收集证据的研究单元，做一次覆盖缺口检查，必要时再启动一个补充单元，最后撰写报告。所有基座模型的检索预算和流程相同，证据空间也相同且不随时间变化。规划、工具使用、证据选择和写作则完全交给模型，每条轨迹都可以审计。",
 "Across the 1,008 trajectories (144 cases × 7 backbones), the number of searches hardly varies, about 10 to 12 per case. Pages read, citations and report length vary a lot, and launching the extra gap unit is only weakly tied to coverage. More activity does not buy more coverage either. On a <em>Horn &amp; Hardart</em> case, GLM 5.2 searches more, opens more pages, reads 112 unique pages to DeepSeek V4 Flash’s 43, uses twice the tokens and writes a longer report, and still covers less on all three metrics.": "在 1,008 条轨迹（144 个样例 × 7 个基座模型）中，检索次数几乎没有差别，每个样例约 10 到 12 次；阅读的页面数、引用数和报告长度则差别很大，是否启动补充单元与覆盖率只有微弱关联。更多的调研活动也不一定带来更高的覆盖率。在一个 <em>Horn &amp; Hardart</em> 样例上，GLM 5.2 检索次数更多，打开的页面更多，读过 112 个不同页面（DeepSeek V4 Flash 为 43 个），消耗的 token 是后者的两倍，报告也更长，三项指标却都更低。",
 "The same metric can also score what an agent <em>retrieved</em>, not just what it wrote. On 24 cases, we score each backbone’s retrieved material and its final report separately. Of the rubric instances fully covered in the retrieved material, <strong>47.0% are no longer fully covered in the report</strong>, and the deeper the knowledge, the more likely it is to be dropped. Models drop different things: DeepSeek V4 Pro keeps more of its depth than its breadth (92.4% vs. 80.4%), DeepSeek V4 Flash the reverse (80.7% vs. 89.9%), and Qwen3.8 Max keeps the most of both, retaining 65.6% of the knowledge it found.": "同一指标还可以用来评估智能体<em>检索到</em>的内容，而不仅是它写出的内容。我们在 24 个样例上分别对每个基座模型的检索材料和最终报告评分。检索材料中完全覆盖的评分细则，有 <strong>47.0% 在报告中不再完全覆盖</strong>，且知识越深，越容易被丢掉。不同模型丢掉的内容也不同：DeepSeek V4 Pro 保留的深度多于广度（92.4% 对 80.4%），DeepSeek V4 Flash 正好相反（80.7% 对 89.9%），Qwen3.8 Max 两方面都保留得最多，检索到的知识有 65.6% 进入了报告。",
 "<b>Figure 6.</b> Inside the local research framework. <b>Activity vs. coverage</b>: one Horn &amp; Hardart case (paper Table 24); each row is scaled to the larger of the two values. <b>Retrieved → reported</b>: breadth and depth of the retrieved material and of the final report, on 24 cases (paper Table 20). <b>Retention by hop</b>: the share of rubrics fully covered in retrieval that are still fully covered in the report (paper Table 21); the thick line is the mean of the seven backbones.": "<b>图 6：</b>本地研究框架内部的情况。<b>调研活动与覆盖率</b>：一个 Horn &amp; Hardart 样例（对应论文表 24），每行按两者中较大的值缩放。<b>检索 → 报告</b>：24 个样例上检索材料与最终报告的广度和深度（对应论文表 20）。<b>按跳数的保留率</b>：检索中完全覆盖的评分细则在报告中仍完全覆盖的比例（对应论文表 21），粗线为七个基座模型的平均。",
 "These differences are not just a matter of length. When all seven backbones are asked for about 1,200 words, the gaps remain: Qwen3.8 Max and DeepSeek V4 Pro write almost the same length (1,198 and 1,239 words) and still differ by 5.24 points. The harness matters too. LangChain’s Open Deep Research, run with DeepSeek V4 Flash and a much larger search budget, reaches 57.11% overall coverage on a 24-case subset, against 45.43% for the same backbone in our local framework.": "这些差异并非只由报告长度造成。要求七个基座模型都写约 1,200 词时，差距依然存在：Qwen3.8 Max 和 DeepSeek V4 Pro 的报告长度几乎相同（1,198 词和 1,239 词），得分仍相差 5.24 个百分点。研究框架同样有影响：LangChain 的 Open Deep Research 搭配 DeepSeek V4 Flash，并使用大得多的检索预算，在 24 个样例的子集上总体覆盖率达到 57.11%，而同一基座模型在我们的本地框架中为 45.43%。",
 "<span class=\"n\">7</span>Can the scores be trusted?": "<span class=\"n\">7</span>评分是否可信",
 "Every number above rests on a judge model reading long reports against hundreds of rubrics, and on a metric with four parameters. We checked both, along with the tasks themselves.": "上述所有数字都依赖评判模型对照数百条评分细则阅读长篇报告，也依赖一个含四个参数的指标。我们对这两方面以及任务本身都做了检验。",
 "<strong>Judge against humans.</strong> On 3,695 rubric judgments from 12 reports, one per domain, we compare three judges with human-reviewed labels. Collapsing the verdicts to covered or not covered gives higher Macro-F1 than keeping three levels, for all three judges. Gemini 2.5 Pro agrees best (0.893 binary), so it is the judge, with its three-level outputs mapped to binary coverage.": "<strong>评判模型与人工标注。</strong>在 12 份报告（每个领域一份）的 3,695 条评分细则判定上，我们将三个评判模型与人工审核的标签比较。对三个评判模型而言，把判定合并为“覆盖”与“未覆盖”两类，Macro-F1 都高于保留三级判定。Gemini 2.5 Pro 一致性最高（二值 0.893），因此被选为评判模型，其三级判定映射为二值覆盖。",
 "<strong>Metric against experts.</strong> Three experts independently rated 72 reports (six agents on 12 cases) for breadth, depth and overall quality. Holding the judge’s verdicts fixed, the structured metrics rank the reports within each case closer to the experts than flat or level-balanced coverage does (Kendall τ<sub>b</sub> 0.751 vs. 0.508 for overall). Removing descendant fusion from breadth or the continuity discount from depth lowers agreement.": "<strong>指标与专家评价。</strong>三位专家独立为 72 份报告（12 个样例上的 6 个智能体）的广度、深度和整体质量打分。在评判结果固定的前提下，结构化指标在每个样例内给出的报告排序比平铺覆盖和按层均衡覆盖都更接近专家（总体维度 Kendall τ<sub>b</sub> 为 0.751，平铺覆盖为 0.508）。去掉广度中的后代融合项或深度中的连续性折扣，一致性都会下降。",
 "<strong>Rankings against parameter choices.</strong> Moving each of β, α, η and ρ up and down changes the agent rankings very little: Spearman correlations with the default stay at least 0.997 for breadth and 0.976 for depth. Depth is most sensitive to α, which causes at most two practical reversals among 120 agent pairs.": "<strong>排名与参数选择。</strong>分别上调和下调 β、α、η、ρ，智能体排名几乎不变：与默认参数下排名的 Spearman 相关系数，广度不低于 0.997，深度不低于 0.976。深度对 α 最敏感，在 120 对智能体中最多出现两次实质性的排名反转。",
 "<b>Figure 7.</b> Validation. <b>Experts</b>: Kendall τ<sub>b</sub> between scores and mean expert ratings, computed within each case and averaged (paper Table 5). <b>Judges</b>: Macro-F1 against human-reviewed labels (paper Table 6). <b>Parameters</b>: Spearman correlation between each perturbed ranking and the default one (paper Table 7); note the axis starts at 0.97.": "<b>图 7：</b>有效性检验。<b>专家</b>：指标得分与专家平均评分之间的 Kendall τ<sub>b</sub>，在每个样例内计算后取平均（对应论文表 5）。<b>评判模型</b>：与人工审核标签相比的 Macro-F1（对应论文表 6）。<b>参数</b>：各参数扰动后的排名与默认排名之间的 Spearman 相关系数（对应论文表 7），注意横轴从 0.97 开始。",
 "The tasks hold up as well. We read all 144 queries: every one is worth a research report and answerable from public sources, and 141 fit their assigned domain cleanly (the other three overlap neighbouring domains). Checking 7,385 query–entity pairs from 24 cases for hidden entities named in the query found 8 leaks (0.108%), none of them at the first hop. After we rebuilt 10 cases with Kimi K2.6 instead of Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Opus 5 still achieved the highest mean overall coverage. Its lead over the models that had scored relatively close to it in the original evaluation narrowed.": "任务本身也经得起检验。我们逐一审阅了全部 144 个研究问题：每个都值得写成研究报告，都能依据公开资料回答，其中 141 个与所属领域完全吻合，其余 3 个与相邻领域有所交叉。在 24 个样例的 7,385 组问题–实体对中检查问题是否直接点出隐藏实体，共发现 8 处泄露（0.108%），且没有一处位于第一跳。改用 Kimi K2.6 替代 Claude Opus 4.8 重建 10 个样例后，与原评测中得分相对接近的几个模型相比，Claude Opus 5 的平均总体覆盖得分仍然最高，只是领先幅度有所缩小。",
 "<span class=\"n\">8</span>Evaluate your own agent": "<span class=\"n\">8</span>评测自己的智能体",
 "The benchmark, judge prompts, evaluator and metrics are released, and the bundled framework is optional. Give each query in <code>queries.jsonl</code> to your agent and save one report per case. Then:": "基准数据、评判提示词、评测程序和指标均已公开，附带的研究框架可选用。将 <code>queries.jsonl</code> 中的每个问题交给待评测的智能体，每个样例保存一份报告，然后运行：",
 "Keep <code>cases.jsonl</code>, which holds the rubrics and the reference trees, away from the agent writing the reports. The paper’s judge is Gemini 2.5 Pro; any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works, but keep the judge fixed when comparing systems. The local research framework is also released as a Docker image with the fixed Wikipedia index, for testing backbones under the controlled setting.": "<code>cases.jsonl</code> 包含评分细则和参考知识树，不要让撰写报告的智能体接触到它。论文使用的评判模型是 Gemini 2.5 Pro；任何兼容 OpenAI 接口的服务都可以使用，但比较不同系统时应保持评判模型不变。本地研究框架也以 Docker 镜像形式发布，内置固定的维基百科索引，可用于在受控条件下测试基座模型。",
 "<strong>Measure where a report covers, not just how much.</strong> Breadth and depth rank the 16 agents differently, and single cases with near-identical scores can hide opposite strategies.": "<strong>评测报告覆盖了哪里，而不只是覆盖了多少。</strong>广度和深度给出的 16 个智能体排名并不相同，分数几乎相同的单个样例也可能对应截然相反的调研策略。",
 "<strong>The workflow shapes the profile.</strong> The same model gains 15.54 breadth points when a research workflow plans and checks for gaps around it.": "<strong>研究流程决定覆盖特征。</strong>同一个模型在加入规划与缺口检查的研究流程后，广度提高了 15.54 个百分点。",
 "<strong>Finding is not reporting.</strong> Nearly half of the knowledge an agent fully retrieves does not survive into its report, and deeper knowledge is lost most.": "<strong>检索到不等于写进报告。</strong>智能体完全检索到的知识，有近一半没有进入最终报告，越深的知识丢失越多。",
 "The case studies, trajectory statistics, cost accounting and every prompt are in the paper’s appendix; the benchmark, evaluator and framework are on <a class=\"tx\" href=\"https://github.com/ZJU-REAL/DRBenchPro\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub</a> and <a class=\"tx\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/zhuiluozhiji/DRBenchPro\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Hugging Face</a>, and the leaderboard is on the <a class=\"tx\" href=\"https://zjureal.com/DRBenchPro/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">project page</a>.": "案例分析、轨迹统计、成本核算和全部提示词见论文附录；基准、评测程序和研究框架发布在 <a class=\"tx\" href=\"https://github.com/ZJU-REAL/DRBenchPro\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub</a> 和 <a class=\"tx\" href=\"https://huggingface.co/datasets/zhuiluozhiji/DRBenchPro\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Hugging Face</a>，排行榜见<a class=\"tx\" href=\"https://zjureal.com/DRBenchPro/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">项目主页</a>。",
 "Animated drawing: ink rays of different lengths grow from one root dot across a torn paper fan, some short and some long, while faint dashed rays mark directions left uncovered": "动画插图：粗细一致的墨线从同一个根点出发，在撕边纸扇上延伸出长短不一的射线，射线上缀有圆点；淡淡的虚线表示未覆盖的方向",
 "Example report": "示例报告",
 "View": "视图",
 "Row order": "行排序",
 "Check": "检验项",
 "DRBench Pro: Measuring the Breadth and Depth of Deep Research · REAL Lab Blog": "DRBench Pro: Measuring the Breadth and Depth of Deep Research · REAL Lab 博客",
 "DRBench Pro scores deep research reports by structured knowledge coverage: 144 Wikipedia-derived cases in 24 domains, 44,102 hidden rubrics placed on knowledge trees, and separate breadth and depth metrics. Sixteen agents evaluated.": "DRBench Pro 以结构化知识覆盖评价深度研究报告：24 个领域的 144 个维基百科样例，44,102 条挂在知识树上的隐藏评分细则，分别计算广度与深度。共评测 16 个智能体。",
 "Two reports can satisfy the same number of rubrics and still be very different: wide and shallow, or narrow and deep. DRBench Pro measures breadth and depth separately.": "两份报告满足的评分细则数量相同，内容却可能一份宽而浅、一份窄而深。DRBench Pro 分别衡量广度与深度。",
 "Two reports can satisfy the same number of rubrics and still be wide and shallow or narrow and deep. 144 Wikipedia-derived cases with hidden rubric trees score breadth and depth separately; the best of 16 agents covers 57.04%.": "两份报告满足的评分细则数量相同，却可能一份宽而浅、一份窄而深。DRBench Pro 以 144 个维基百科样例和隐藏的评分细则树分别衡量广度与深度，16 个智能体中最好的总体覆盖率为 57.04%。"
}